<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Latvians</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Letts</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Latvians are a Baltic people native to Latvia, speaking Latvian, one of the two surviving Baltic languages. They formed from the merging of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latgalians">Latgalians</a>, Selonians, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/semigallians">Semigallians</a> and Curonians with assimilated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonians">Livonians</a>, under centuries of German, Polish, Swedish and Russian rule. A national awakening in the 19th century led to the founding of the independent Republic of Latvia in 1918.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/latvians.jpg" alt="Latvians" width="320" height="144" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Allice Hunter · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_the_Latvian_Diaspora_in_the_World.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
